1.1.text:
Article 3

The objectives of the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence and Trafficking in Persons are:

a. To protect women and children victims of violence and trafficking in persons;
b. To take action against perpetrators of violence and trafficking in persons against women and children;
c. To provide a sense of security to women and children victims of violence and trafficking in persons;
d. To restore the physical, psychological, social, and economic conditions of women and children victims of violence and trafficking in persons.
e. To ensure the existence of comprehensive services in implementing policies, programs and activities for the protection of women and children victims of violence and trafficking in persons.

Article 21

The Regent in implementing policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women and children who are victims of violence and human trafficking, makes efforts to:

a. coordinate the implementation of policies, programs, and activities among SKPD;
b. cooperate with other regencies and cities within one province, and with regencies and cities in other provinces, in the implementation of policies, programs and activities in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
c. facilitate and provide services;
d. implement affirmative action for the protection of women and children and human trafficking; and
e. develop a data system for the protection of women and children, including a data system on violence against women and children and human trafficking.

Article 7

The regional government is obligated and responsible to:

a. implement all efforts to prevent the occurrence of criminal acts of trafficking in persons, and violence against women and children;
b. provide and organize integrated services for victims;
c. ensure the implementation of protection for victims by taking into account the rights and obligations of parents, guardians, husbands or other persons legally responsible for the victim;
d. supervise the implementation of services to victims, with service standards that involve the community;
e. Open the widest possible access to information to the community, especially to women and children victims of violence and trafficking in persons.

Article 8

The community participates to:

a. carry out efforts to prevent the occurrence of criminal acts of trafficking in persons and violence;
b. supervise and report the occurrence of criminal acts of trafficking in persons and violence to the competent authorities;
c. propose formulation and policies regarding protection; d. make efforts to protect and provide moral and/or material support to victims.

Article 4

Every victim has the right to:

a. receive protection from individuals, groups or regional governments as well as private institutions;
b. receive information about the existence of complaint centers, KPPA, companions, social workers and spiritual counselors, psychologists and psychiatrists, from individuals, groups, or government, regional government and national and international private institutions;
c. receive integrated services in accordance with applicable legislation;
d. make claims and/or lawsuits through judicial bodies, and may report to the International Court;
e. receive restitution or compensation payments;
f. receive information about legislation that protects victims;
g. special handling related to victim confidentiality;
h. receive information and be involved in every decision-making process related to accompaniment and case service development;
i. receive guarantees for their rights related to their status as wife, mother or child and household member, as well as community member;
j. receive psychological, medical, spiritual and legal assistance at every level of examination and during the judicial process;
k. receive continuous handling up to the rehabilitation and reintegration stage.

Article 14

(1) Assistance includes all integrated efforts to restore and strengthen the condition of victims carried out by the Police, Prosecutor's Office, Court, Advocates and social workers, Women's Crisis Center, women's and social organizations concerned with women and children;

(2) Assistance by the police, prosecutor's office, court, and advocates as referred to in paragraph (1) is in accordance with legislation.

Article 2

The principles in the protection of women and children victims of violence and trafficking in persons are:

a. Legal Certainty;
b. Justice and Gender Equality;
c. Non-discrimination;
d. Best interests of victims;
e. Respect for the rights of women and children as the fulfillment of Human Rights.

Article 5

Restitution or compensation payments as referred to in article 4 letter e include:

a. loss of wealth or income;
b. suffering;
c. costs for medical and/or psychological treatment;
d. other losses suffered by victims as a result of trafficking in persons and violence.

