Article 15

(1) The duties of Social Workers as companions are:

a. provide sufficient information to victims about their rights;
b. establish an equal relationship with victims so they are willing to open up in expressing their problems;
c. ask what they want to do and what assistance is needed;
d. provide information and connect with institutions or individuals who can help overcome problems;
e. provide information about legal consultation services; f. accompany victims during the medicological process;
g. accompany victims during the examination process at the Police, Prosecutor's Office, and Court;
h. monitor the interests and rights of victims in the examination process at the Police, Prosecutor's Office, and Court;
i. maintain the privacy and confidentiality of victims from all parties who have no interest, including coverage by mass media;
j. coordinate with other companions;
k. provide continuous handling up to the rehabilitation and reintegration stage
(2) Services to victims are carried out in an integrated and continuous manner by service providers.

